    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head>Af Rb 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>IIII. Be borgbryce.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Rubrics-Af_3.lnote.oe.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-ot-frag"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>… rhbryce.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-g-prol"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>IIII. Be burhbryce.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Rubrics-Af_3.lnote.oe.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>IIII. Be burhbryce.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>De infractione plegii.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Rubrics-Af_3.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="186" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>IIII Be borgbryce</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>Von Verletzung des Bürgschaftsschutzes.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rubrics-Af_3.lnote.de.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of the violation of surety-protection.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="187" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning breach of security</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">17</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">regis <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">regis added by Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">16</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">borhb. <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">borhb. So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_3.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">17</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">urh <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">urh on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht der Bürge verletzt sein Wort, sondern er wird gekränkt, indem ein Dritter Verletzung an dem von ihm Verbürgten, Geschützten begeht. ‘Bürgschaftsbruch’ wäre zweideutig. Da <hi rend="italic">borg</hi> im Sinne von ‘Schutz’ im XI. Jh. selten wurde, missverstanden zwei Schreiber GH (ebenso zum Texte von Af 3 Schreiber von Q) <hi rend="italic">burg</hi>: ‘Einbruch (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2d) ins Haus’: ein häufiges Verbrechen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">It is not the surety who breaks his word; rather, he is wronged, in that a third party commits an injury against the person whom he has guaranteed and protected. ‘Breach of surety’ would be ambiguous. Since <hi rend="italic">borg</hi> in the sense of ‘protection’ became rare in the 11th cent., two scribes, GH (and likewise the scribe of Q in the text of Af 3), misread it as <hi rend="italic">burg</hi>: ‘break-in (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2d) at the house’: a common crime</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
